{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_30","type":"agent_message","text":"TorchInductor only wins for the smallest merged batch: at M=128 it selects a Triton GEMM tile (`64×64×256`) and beats the vendor path by about 7%; at M≥1024 the verified hipBLASLt route remains faster. I’m reproducing that small-M tile directly with a fused bias, BF16 rounding, and exact GELU epilogue, avoiding Inductor’s heavy per-shape compilation and keeping the existing path for larger batches."}}
