{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_35","type":"agent_message","text":"The direct small-M GEMM lowers the M=128 end-to-end path from about 0.095 ms to 0.085 ms and remains fully within tolerance. More importantly, using the hardware reciprocal square root in normalization drops the largest front-end stage from 0.19 ms to 0.15 ms. I’m doing one last local occupancy sweep around that faster instruction before the fourth official run."}}
