{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_56","type":"agent_message","text":"The exhaustive hipBLASLt sweep found no material GEMM gain—the best large FC1 solution was only ~0.2% ahead of PyTorch, so I’m keeping the simpler verified vendor path. I’m testing one narrowly scoped improvement to the M=128 Triton epilogue: the standard tanh GELU approximation, whose intrinsic error is far below the workload tolerance and may avoid the costlier `erf`."}}
